  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{2x+10}-4.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{2x+10}-4=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{2x+10}-4 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{2x+10} & =4 \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{2x+10})^{3} & ={4}^{3} \\\\ 2x+10 & =64 \\\\ 2x & =54 \\\\ x & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=27.$",
